// NOTE: the running harness actually loads spicedb-combined.zed (this
// file's content plus spicedb-example.zed's, as one schema write — see
// that file's own doc comment for why). This file stays as the
// standalone, readable reference translation of just the depth-chain
// type.
//
// The depth-scaling check-latency workload's SpiceDB schema — see
// openfga-depth-chain.fga's own doc comment for what this measures and
// why it is a separate, minimal schema rather than an extension of
// spicedb-example.zed.
//
// A plain tuple-to-userset chain (`parent: bench_node`), matching
// openfga-depth-chain.fga's own shape exactly — SpiceDB has no
// restriction against a userset-typed tupleset relation the way OpenFGA
// does (a `relation parent: bench_node | bench_node#member` schema also
// compiles and behaves identically here), but this harness uses the
// identical plain-pointer shape across all three engines' depth-chain
// schemas deliberately, so a latency difference in the results can never
// be blamed on "these two engines walked a structurally different
// rewrite rule than the third."

definition user {}

definition bench_node {
	relation viewer: user
	relation parent: bench_node

	// bench_node.view = viewer | parent->view (this repo's DSL spelling)
	permission view = viewer + parent->view
}
